CORE
main.c
--chain chain.sh
^Reason: invalid loop hash in main\.hash_xyz$
^EXIT=1$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^VERIFICATION
--
A malformed hash-based loop identifier (the hash part is not a number) must be
rejected with an "invalid loop hash" error rather than silently accepted. The
chain.sh passes --unwindset main.hash_xyz:6; cbmc exits with an error before
verification.
